From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:18:30 -0700
Subject: Limit 3D textures to 4Gb when rounded to PoT on IMG

Adds a toggle to throw a synthetic OOM on when the dimensions of
the base level of a 3D texture, rounded to the next power-of-two,
cause the texture level to exceed 4Gb storage size. This works
around a bug on PowerVR GPUs.

Bug: 567735302
Change-Id: Iebd98645c60a9c7ae1a35fef8ff0db3046f7c4c1
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/348055
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

